.TH CFOUTIL 1 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
cfoUtil \- compile or load a CFO run plan, program the CFO clock, show DMA state
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cfoUtil
.RI [ options ]
.BR write_program | program_clock | dma_info
.SH DESCRIPTION
.TP
.B write_program
With
.BR \-C :
compile the source
.B \-p
to
.B \-f
with
.B CFO_Compiler
and exit 0 without touching the card (whether or not
.B \-f
was given, contrary to the usage text).
Without
.BR \-C :
read the binary
.BR \-p ,
prefix its size + 8 as a 64-bit word, and send it as one DAQ-channel DMA
to the CFO.
The file is read into a 64 KiB stack buffer without a size check; a file larger
than 65528 bytes overruns it, and a missing file is reported but the write
proceeds.
.TP
.B program_clock
Set the oscillator to
.B \-F
Hz.
.TP
.B dma_info
Print the driver's ring metadata
.RB ( mu2edev::meta_dump() ).
.PP
.B write_program
(without
.BR \-C )
and
.B program_clock
construct
.B CFO_Registers
in mode
.B DTC_SimMode_NoCFO
without
.BR skipInit ,
which runs the CFO initialisation.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " file"
Input (default
.IR /tmp/cfoUtil.raw ).
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
Compiler output (default
.IR /tmp/cfoUtil.raw ).
.TP
.B \-C
Input is source to compile.
.TP
.BI \-F " Hz"
Frequency for
.B program_clock
(default 166666667).
.TP
.BI \-c " Hz"
CFO clock speed (default 40000000); parsed but not used.
.TP
.BI \-\-cfo " n"
Card index (default
.B DTCLIB_DTC
for
.BR dma_info ;
otherwise
.BR CFOLIB_CFO ,
then
.BR DTCLIB_DTC ,
then 0).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Usage, exit 0; an unknown option also prints the usage and exits 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0, including for an unrecognised operation; library exceptions abort.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.BR CFOLIB_CFO ,
.BR DTCLIB_DTC ,
.BR CFOLIB_SIM_ENABLE ,
.BR DTCLIB_SIM_ENABLE .
.SH FILES
.I /tmp/cfoUtil.raw
\(em default input and output.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
cfoUtil \-C \-p plan.txt \-f plan.bin write_program
cfoUtil \-\-cfo 0 \-p plan.bin write_program
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mu2eCompiler (1),
.BR CFORegDump (1),
.BR libCFOInterface (3)
